  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: Delivery of the Kano Education Recovery Conference</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kano state government of Nigeria is convening an Education Recovery Conference to address the significant challenges in the sector. The theme of the Conference is &#x2018;Repositioning Education in Kano State: Navigating the Path to Excellence&#x2019;. The forum will target leaders, political actors, advocates, and policymakers to design a roadmap to reposition and rebuild education in the state. Deliberations at the conference will address the significant education sector challenges faced in Kano State. The key outcome of the conference would be the development of sustainable solutions that will promote access to quality education for all children in the state, particularly considering recent socioeconomic and security challenges in the state. This conference is a move towards accelerating progress towards achieving Sustainable Development Goal 4 (SDG4), as adopted by the United Nations in 2015. The British Government, working though its Foreign and Commonwealth office, is supporting delivery of the SDGs internationally, through its education programmes in Nigeria and elsewhere.</narrative>
  </description>
